{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S1 T2 CI FAILURE root-caused and fixed (no retry). Gerrit 1883 got LLM-Review +1 but Verified -1; all FOUR pytest jobs failed identically ~10s in, i.e. before pytest ran, so not platform flake. Real cause read from the run log: '##[error]docs/env-vars.md is stale'. That file is GENERATED and records the line numbers of non-literal env reads; deleting persistence code shifted the _env_int read in binding_store.py from line 110 to 109. Regenerated with scripts/gen_env_registry.py - a one-line diff. Notable: line 110 is exactly the _env_int site the coordinator flagged as the RP-04 S7.3.a collision, so its line reference has now moved and that is captured for the retarget ticket. Non-behavioral generated-doc reference, so fixed directly per the skill rather than test-covered. ALSO APPLIED BOTH LLM-Review ADVISORIES - both were legitimate change-detector critiques of MY tests, which is the coupling this skill explicitly forbids: (1) the signature test asserted rendered annotation text, so reformatting str | None to Optional[str] would fail it for no observable reason - it now pins parameter NAMES and KINDS (what callers actually bind to) and additionally guards against drift hidden behind **kwargs, covering more real hazard than before; (2) the ownership test asserted an exact ordered call trace, coupling to delegation mechanism - it now asserts collaborator invocation as MEMBERSHIP plus the observable effects (baseline round-trips through a reload, rotation stamp reaches the sidecar file). Re-verified teeth after both rewrites: SIX defect-seeded mutations all RED (all_bindings deep copy, facade copying the repo document so a top-level insert is lost, repository leaked publicly, parameter rename, **kwargs masking, get_rotation bypassed). PROCESS MISTAKE and lesson: I amended with git commit --amend -F <file> and the message file omitted the Change-Id trailer, so the commit-msg hook minted a NEW one and Gerrit opened change 1885 instead of adding a patch set to 1883. Abandoned 1883 with an explanatory message; 1885 is the live change. From here, any amend that supplies a full message file must carry the existing Change-Id trailer forward."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787102276302716001,"uuid":"97e0c5d1-9b7e-43ae-bebf-2ceeff5a171c"}